  📗
    The path-and-query part of the target, or no value when it has none.
    For an absolute target the authority becomes the Host header, as RFC 9112
    requires an origin server to prefer it.
  📗
  🔒❗️ 🎣 ➡️ 🍬🔡 🍇
    ↪️ 🎼 target 🔤/🔤❗️ 🍇
      ↩️ target
    🍉
    ↪️ 📪🐇🧮 ✂️🐇🧰 target 0 7❗️❗️ 🙌 🔤http://🔤 🍇
      🦶🐇🧰 target 7❗️ ➡️ afterScheme
      📐 afterScheme❗️ ➡️ 🖍🆕end
      ↪️ 🔍 afterScheme 🔤/🔤❗️ ➡️ slash 🍇
        slash ➡️ 🖍end
      🍉
      ↪️ 🔍 afterScheme 🔤?🔤❗️ ➡️ mark 🍇
        ↪️ mark ◀️ end 🍇
          mark ➡️ 🖍end
        🍉
      🍉
      ↪️ end 🙌 0 🍇
        ↩️ 🤷‍♀️
      🍉
      🔖 headers 🔤Host🔤 ✂️🐇🧰 afterScheme 0 end❗️❗️
      🦶🐇🧰 afterScheme end❗️ ➡️ rest
      ↪️ 🎼 rest 🔤/🔤❗️ 🍇
        ↩️ rest
      🍉
      ↩️ 🔤/🧲rest🧲🔤
    🍉
    ↩️ 🤷‍♀️
