  📗
    Turns *rawPath* into decoded segments. Dot segments are resolved before
    decoding and each segment is decoded on its own, so an encoded slash or
    an encoded dot can never change which route matches.
  📗
  🔒❗️ 🧗 rawPath 🔡 ➡️ 👌 🍇
    🆕🍨🐚🔡🍆❗️ ➡️ 🖍🆕kept
    🔂 part 🔫 rawPath 🔤/🔤❗️ 🍇
      ↪️ part 🙌 🔤..🔤 🍇
        ↪️ 📏 kept❓ 🙌 0 🍇
          🔤the path climbs above the root🔤 ➡️ 🖍problem
          ↩️ 👎
        🍉
        🐼 kept❗️
      🍉
      🙅↪️ ❎ 🤜part 🙌 🔤🔤 👐 part 🙌 🔤.🔤🤛❗️ 🍇
        🐻 kept part❗️
      🍉
    🍉
    🆕🍨🐚🔡🍆❗️ ➡️ 🖍🆕decoded
    🔂 part kept 🍇
      ↪️ 🧹🐇🧰 part❗️ ➡️ text 🍇
        ↪️ text 🙌 🔤.🔤 👐 text 🙌 🔤..🔤 🍇
          🔤the path has an encoded dot segment🔤 ➡️ 🖍problem
          ↩️ 👎
        🍉
        🐻 decoded text❗️
      🍉
      🙅 🍇
        🔤the path has a bad percent-escape🔤 ➡️ 🖍problem
        ↩️ 👎
      🍉
    🍉
    decoded ➡️ 🖍segments
    🆕🔡 decoded 🔤/🔤❗️ ➡️ joined
    🔤/🧲joined🧲🔤 ➡️ 🖍path
    ↩️ 👍
